-- A diamond of aliases 300 deep: `A{i} a` is `A{i-1} (A{i-1} a)`. The inner
-- application of each level costs two levels of the type reader, so a read
-- of `A300 Int` passes the reader's bound, 512, near `A44`. An expansion
-- that ran out of depth is not shared, and each level above the bound was
-- expanded again, so this file did not end (#2124). A read that ran out of
-- depth now expands no more aliases (checker-v2.md §7.4, amended
-- 2026-11-27).
--
-- The messages are the ones that a diamond 260 deep gave before, except
-- for `g`. The depth is reported at the public constructor (`Shown`), at
-- the annotations (`f`, `g`) and at the used constructor (`Used 1 2`). The
-- part of each type that the reader did read stays in use: `"s"` is not
-- `Int`, and `2` is not `String`. `g`'s result is the alias `Name`, after
-- the too-deep part. The reader does not expand it now, so `g`'s body lost
-- its mismatch against `Name`. `Unused`, a private constructor that nothing
-- calls, gets no message (`check/good/AliasDiamondTooDeepUnused`).
type alias A0 a =
    a


type alias A1 a =
    A0 (A0 a)


type alias A2 a =
    A1 (A1 a)


type alias A3 a =
    A2 (A2 a)


